{"title":"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of consecutive positive integers beginning with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is written on a blackboard. One number is erased. The average (arithmetic mean) of the remaining numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b62219f800cb0c95765588391bac8d02cd1b712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35\\frac{7}{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />. What number was erased? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e545bd5058e9a711b0d44536dad403a1a30ba6cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ 7 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 8 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\  9\\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{cannot be determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"500\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers in the set initially, so their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f8070867b03b0dc224db7e741135e07f4502c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" /> by arithmetic series. The average of the remaining numbers is minimized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is erased, and is maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is erased.\n</p><p>It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea0b84f7cf916258a52e571a45582ab49c12f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> We write and solve a compound inequality for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d5dbb87dfb42bdebf7025f8c5eb7243c949aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n:$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94ee538e5dd9872fe55058ef64502869ab50d5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} \\frac{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-n}{n-1} &amp;\\leq 35\\frac{7}{17} &amp;&amp;\\leq \\frac{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-1}{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{n(n+1)-2n}{2(n-1)} &amp;\\leq 35\\frac{7}{17} &amp;&amp;\\leq \\frac{n(n+1)-2}{2(n-1)} \\\\ \\frac{n^2-n}{2(n-1)} &amp;\\leq 35\\frac{7}{17} &amp;&amp;\\leq \\frac{n^2+n-2}{2(n-1)} \\\\ \\frac{n(n-1)}{2(n-1)} &amp;\\leq 35\\frac{7}{17} &amp;&amp;\\leq \\frac{(n+2)(n-1)}{2(n-1)} \\\\ \\frac{n}{2} &amp;\\leq 35\\frac{7}{17} &amp;&amp;\\leq \\frac{n+2}{2} \\\\ n &amp;\\leq 70\\frac{14}{17} &amp;&amp;\\leq n+2 \\\\ 68\\frac{14}{17} &amp;\\leq \\hspace{3mm} n &amp;&amp;\\leq 70\\frac{14}{17}, \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"315\" height=\"323\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80952a9a250e7257f7c6d64e763dae189dbb271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/8/df8f84ec7aa690c07175434b64b9ea581403ad54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number that is erased. We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca3dd6894864f1189a98ab606fc2654542828946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-x}{n-1}=35\\frac{7}{17},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"156\" height=\"46\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72dd7c4d56c373adc964be1cafa3ad9c3ee91760.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-x=35\\frac{7}{17}\\cdot(n-1). \\hspace{15mm}(\\bigstar)\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5dd19e106c3373f54fca2fb6e50138d7ee09917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=70,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268602cef530d5fb3aec0ddff121739eb1f983e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2485-x=\\frac{41538}{17},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de6f2e0a5e210c361f8a41acfc391686d7638fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{707}{17},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" /> contradicting the precondition that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e76a00c8fdb0a15c502b02e6926936e996c35ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=69,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/69852e9dc5cba58023327ddcc24e38e29476b62d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2415-x=2408,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a742ac5d10f62bd6bfa5eec54ba86414a349190e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"96\" height=\"30\" /></li></ul>\n<p><u><b>Remark</b></u>\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458f4c22e3fa988062d6b0856b2d421bf939f7d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> note that the left side must be an integer, so must be the right side. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6f366f39bfe4c4ef43c2853a1e2f1557e4423b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/8382f87b45c2c6399324df8f68f1fd51b9361635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=69.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME\" title=\"1982 AHSME\">1982 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1982 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1982\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a h